1
00:00:06,974 --> 00:00:10,274
I received this because I passed
your test, Iorygoi-san.

2
00:00:10,274 --> 00:00:12,074
It's a very precious bottle.

3
00:00:12,544 --> 00:00:19,034
When the bottle is filled to the brim, that's
when I can go to the place of my wishes.

4
00:00:19,644 --> 00:00:20,944
Right, Ioryogi-san?

5
00:00:21,484 --> 00:00:23,854
When do you think it will fill up?

6
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:26,384
I can't wait, can you?

7
00:00:26,584 --> 00:00:28,314
Let's get this straight...

8
00:00:29,324 --> 00:00:32,454
You are the one who is going to fill it, Kobato!

9
00:00:37,634 --> 00:00:40,774
Kobato.

10
00:00:40,774 --> 00:00:43,604
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

11
00:00:43,604 --> 00:00:48,004
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

12
00:00:48,914 --> 00:00:52,214
Muzukashii na

13
00:00:52,214 --> 00:00:54,984
Ureshii toki waratte

14
00:00:54,984 --> 00:00:59,284
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

15
00:00:59,854 --> 00:01:02,294
Na no ni

16
00:01:03,594 --> 00:01:07,964
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

17
00:01:08,394 --> 00:01:11,664
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

18
00:01:11,664 --> 00:01:15,164
Machikirenai yo

19
00:01:15,304 --> 00:01:21,074
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

20
00:01:21,074 --> 00:01:26,284
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

21
00:01:26,284 --> 00:01:29,114
Doko ni aru no?

22
00:01:29,114 --> 00:01:32,454
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

23
00:01:32,454 --> 00:01:35,294
Meippai kizu tsuite

24
00:01:35,294 --> 00:01:38,194
Seiippai hashitte

25
00:01:38,194 --> 00:01:42,164
Nan juu kai koronde naite

26
00:01:42,164 --> 00:01:45,204
Sore de mo mada

27
00:01:45,204 --> 00:01:49,224
Akireru kurai

28
00:01:49,704 --> 00:01:53,874
Ashita wo shinjiteru

29
00:02:03,114 --> 00:02:04,514
Hanato Kobato!

30
00:02:04,684 --> 00:02:05,774
Yes sir!

31
00:02:05,954 --> 00:02:07,024
...The Shining Kompeito.
Now listen!

32
00:02:07,024 --> 00:02:09,524
...The Shining Kompeito.
Nothing is going to happen with that bottle,
unless you do something about it!

33
00:02:09,524 --> 00:02:10,724
...The Shining Kompeito.
What is it that you're going to fill it with?!

34
00:02:10,724 --> 00:02:11,594
What is it that you're going to fill it with?!

35
00:02:11,964 --> 00:02:15,764
Sir! I'm going to fill it with
people's broken hearts, sir!

36
00:02:15,764 --> 00:02:17,394
And how are you going to collect those hearts?!

37
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:22,134
Sir! I must heal those broken hearts first, sir!

38
00:02:22,604 --> 00:02:25,764
Good. As long as you understand.

39
00:02:26,104 --> 00:02:27,974
Well then, we have no time to waste!

40
00:02:27,974 --> 00:02:28,944
Yes sir!

41
00:02:28,944 --> 00:02:30,774
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

42
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:35,414
Don't talk to me when humans are nearby.

43
00:02:35,654 --> 00:02:37,724
Huh? Why am I not allowed?

44
00:02:37,724 --> 00:02:41,714
I'm only going to explain this to you,
since you obviously lack in memory,

45
00:02:42,154 --> 00:02:44,594
knowledge and common sense,
but here, stuffed toys don't talk.

46
00:02:44,894 --> 00:02:47,634
Talking to things that don't
talk is considered strange.

47
00:02:47,634 --> 00:02:48,994
Do you understand?!

48
00:02:50,464 --> 00:02:52,434
Why don't they talk?

49
00:02:52,804 --> 00:02:54,704
Because they are stuffed toys.

50
00:02:56,134 --> 00:02:59,194
Why does being a stuffed toy
keep them from talking?

51
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:03,244
Never mind, just go!

52
00:03:03,244 --> 00:03:05,874
Okay! Kobato is ready!

53
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:12,614
Why did you have to jump off the seesaw?!

54
00:03:13,824 --> 00:03:16,124
Anybody with a broken heart?

55
00:03:17,194 --> 00:03:19,494
Anybody who would like to be healed?

56
00:03:19,694 --> 00:03:22,394
Anybody with a broken heart?

57
00:03:23,764 --> 00:03:26,134
Please let me heal your heart!

58
00:03:26,334 --> 00:03:27,994
I-I'm good, thanks...

59
00:03:28,534 --> 00:03:31,934
Excuse me! Isn't there something I
can help you with healing?

60
00:03:32,444 --> 00:03:33,704
Oh, give me a break.

61
00:03:34,974 --> 00:03:36,774
Is there something I can help you with?!

62
00:03:36,774 --> 00:03:38,544
Rock, paper, scissors.
Is there something I can help you with?!

63
00:03:38,544 --> 00:03:40,174
Rock, paper...

64
00:03:41,684 --> 00:03:43,244
Can you help us?

65
00:03:43,854 --> 00:03:45,024
Sure, what can I do for you?

66
00:03:45,024 --> 00:03:46,954
Can you be "it" for kick the can?

67
00:03:47,024 --> 00:03:50,654
It? I can help you by being "it"?

68
00:03:50,994 --> 00:03:52,514
Yes! Please?

69
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:54,924
Okay! I'll do my best!

70
00:03:56,164 --> 00:03:57,634
I kicked the can!

71
00:04:23,524 --> 00:04:27,154
Huh? That's funny. The bottle is still empty.

72
00:04:27,464 --> 00:04:30,154
What were you going to heal by
being it in kick the can?

73
00:04:30,234 --> 00:04:33,464
Where are you going to find a heart
that needs healing that way?

74
00:04:33,934 --> 00:04:35,334
Did I do something wrong?

75
00:04:35,574 --> 00:04:38,874
All you were doing was being their playmate.

76
00:04:39,504 --> 00:04:41,444
Really...

77
00:04:42,174 --> 00:04:47,174
I guess it's not easy running into
someone who needs healing.

78
00:04:49,854 --> 00:04:50,954
But, but!

79
00:04:50,954 --> 00:04:53,224
The fact that there's nobody out
there that needs healing

80
00:04:53,224 --> 00:04:57,884
means that there's nobody out there that's hurt
or feeling sad, which is a good thing.

81
00:04:59,124 --> 00:05:02,424
Is there no limit to your positive thinking?

82
00:05:02,994 --> 00:05:05,434
Yomogi Station

83
00:05:06,804 --> 00:05:10,464
I just hope I can find a way to help.

84
00:05:10,874 --> 00:05:12,774
Uh... h-hi...

85
00:05:15,214 --> 00:05:16,974
Uh... p-please...

86
00:05:18,914 --> 00:05:21,144
This is... for me?

87
00:05:21,554 --> 00:05:23,454
Uh, yes. Please take it.

88
00:05:23,684 --> 00:05:29,184
To be able to give strangers something so
special, without the slightest bit of hesitation.

89
00:05:29,524 --> 00:05:31,614
What a wonderful person!

90
00:05:32,164 --> 00:05:33,594
Oh, come on.

91
00:05:34,134 --> 00:05:36,694
I still have this much more to hand out.

92
00:05:37,104 --> 00:05:39,724
It would be a great help if you
could take as many as you like.

93
00:05:39,904 --> 00:05:41,304
Really?!

94
00:05:41,304 --> 00:05:43,294
Then I'll take them all!

95
00:05:43,374 --> 00:05:44,104
Huh?

96
00:05:46,674 --> 00:05:49,044
Wow, thanks! You saved me!

97
00:05:49,274 --> 00:05:53,074
I was able to help him out and
look what I got in return!

98
00:05:53,244 --> 00:05:56,114
Now what are you going to do with all that?

99
00:05:57,084 --> 00:06:01,924
Now it's my turn to give out
these wonderful gifts!

100
00:06:02,894 --> 00:06:03,854
Huh?

101
00:06:05,724 --> 00:06:08,324
Here you are! Aren't these terrific tissues?

102
00:06:08,794 --> 00:06:11,324
They'll come in handy, I promise. Here!

103
00:06:11,664 --> 00:06:15,464
Here! Here! Here! Here!

104
00:06:16,204 --> 00:06:17,874
I'll give you as many as you like!

105
00:06:17,874 --> 00:06:19,844
Uh... I'm good... thanks.

106
00:06:20,144 --> 00:06:22,704
Go ahead! There's no need to hesitate.

107
00:06:22,974 --> 00:06:24,744
Please! Here!

108
00:06:24,944 --> 00:06:27,214
Have a pack of lovely tissues! Please!

109
00:06:31,324 --> 00:06:32,544
That hurt.

110
00:06:33,084 --> 00:06:34,714
I-I'm sorry!

111
00:06:35,994 --> 00:06:36,854
Hey.

112
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:38,064
Yes!

113
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:40,584
Stop wandering around in
the middle of the street.

114
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:42,524
I'm sorry!

115
00:06:46,464 --> 00:06:47,804
That guy...

116
00:06:48,734 --> 00:06:50,064
From the other day...

117
00:06:50,904 --> 00:06:52,874
Pick up those tissues, would you?

118
00:06:57,544 --> 00:07:01,644
Please wait! Um, I need to thank you!

119
00:07:09,494 --> 00:07:12,324
I'm sure he came this way.

120
00:07:16,864 --> 00:07:18,464
The sheet flew off!

121
00:07:18,464 --> 00:07:20,434
Over here, Ms. Sayaka!

122
00:07:22,534 --> 00:07:23,834
What are you doing?

123
00:07:24,074 --> 00:07:25,504
Oh my goodness!

124
00:07:27,374 --> 00:07:28,704
Are you alright?

125
00:07:29,044 --> 00:07:30,204
Yes...

126
00:07:30,544 --> 00:07:32,344
She scratched her nose!

127
00:07:32,344 --> 00:07:33,444
Huh?!

128
00:07:33,754 --> 00:07:35,014
You're right!

129
00:07:35,954 --> 00:07:37,684
I'm so embarrassed!

130
00:07:37,824 --> 00:07:39,844
You two! That was impolite.

131
00:07:40,024 --> 00:07:42,284
Yes, Teacher Sayaka.

132
00:07:42,894 --> 00:07:43,994
I'm so sorry.

133
00:07:43,994 --> 00:07:47,124
I work here at Yomogi Kindergarten.

134
00:07:47,194 --> 00:07:50,924
We're understaffed you see, so we got
delayed in bringing the laundry in.

135
00:07:52,664 --> 00:07:54,374
You don't have enough people?!

136
00:07:54,374 --> 00:07:56,064
Ah, that's right.

137
00:07:56,904 --> 00:07:58,334
Is that a problem?!

138
00:07:58,844 --> 00:08:00,104
Y-You could say so.

139
00:08:00,304 --> 00:08:02,274
Would it help if you had enough people?!

140
00:08:02,574 --> 00:08:03,844
Well...

141
00:08:03,844 --> 00:08:05,404
Would it help?!

142
00:08:06,084 --> 00:08:07,344
Uh, y-yes!

143
00:08:09,584 --> 00:08:10,984
I will help you!

144
00:08:10,984 --> 00:08:12,014
Huh?

145
00:08:14,154 --> 00:08:15,314
Uh, this is for you!

146
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:21,254
Thank you.

147
00:08:25,534 --> 00:08:27,524
So, what's your name?

148
00:08:27,974 --> 00:08:29,264
I'm Toshihiko!

149
00:08:29,504 --> 00:08:31,704
My name is Kobato Hanato.

150
00:08:31,974 --> 00:08:34,734
Kobato? What a weird name.

151
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:36,434
What a weird name!

152
00:08:39,614 --> 00:08:41,174
Do you think so?

153
00:08:41,484 --> 00:08:43,884
Then your father's name must be Obato!

154
00:08:43,884 --> 00:08:45,514
Well it isn't.

155
00:08:45,624 --> 00:08:47,144
Then what is it?

156
00:08:47,424 --> 00:08:48,784
What is it?!

157
00:08:49,624 --> 00:08:50,224
Uh, well...

158
00:08:50,224 --> 00:08:50,794
His name.
Uh, well...

159
00:08:50,794 --> 00:08:51,224
His name.

160
00:08:51,224 --> 00:08:52,364
What's his name?

161
00:08:52,364 --> 00:08:53,624
Come on.

162
00:08:54,064 --> 00:08:56,324
What is it? Tell me.

163
00:08:56,694 --> 00:08:57,754
Hey.

164
00:09:01,074 --> 00:09:02,604
Yes?

165
00:09:02,604 --> 00:09:05,634
Do you... not have a father?

166
00:09:07,514 --> 00:09:08,844
Probably not.

167
00:09:11,544 --> 00:09:13,014
Never mind about the name.

168
00:09:13,014 --> 00:09:13,954
Right.

169
00:09:13,954 --> 00:09:16,314
Come on, let's play! Come on!

170
00:09:16,314 --> 00:09:18,844
Now children, don't be causing trouble.

171
00:09:18,984 --> 00:09:21,584
Yes, Ms. Sayaka!

172
00:09:22,124 --> 00:09:25,094
Oh, I would like to help with something.

173
00:09:25,394 --> 00:09:28,884
You'd be a great help just carrying on
with the children like you were.

174
00:09:30,234 --> 00:09:33,934
Carrying on? Uh, well...

175
00:09:33,934 --> 00:09:35,334
Miss Kobato?

176
00:09:35,834 --> 00:09:37,004
Yes?

177
00:09:37,004 --> 00:09:38,434
Play the organ!

178
00:09:38,844 --> 00:09:42,744
I'm sorry, I don't know how to play the organ.

179
00:09:43,314 --> 00:09:44,814
Is that so.

180
00:09:44,814 --> 00:09:49,014
I'm sorry. But I can dance with you.

181
00:09:49,184 --> 00:09:50,384
You dance?

182
00:09:50,384 --> 00:09:51,624
Yes!

183
00:09:51,624 --> 00:09:52,744
Wait here, okay?

184
00:09:54,854 --> 00:09:57,954
Mr. Kiyokazu, will you play the organ?

185
00:09:59,294 --> 00:10:00,354
Oh!

186
00:10:03,964 --> 00:10:06,294
I wanna dance with Teacher Kobato.

187
00:10:06,704 --> 00:10:08,934
She's no teacher.

188
00:10:09,104 --> 00:10:11,194
Then just plain Kobato!

189
00:10:11,874 --> 00:10:15,114
What's the big idea? You followed me here.

190
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:19,044
Huh? I just wanted to thank you properly.

191
00:10:20,084 --> 00:10:21,844
Never mind. Go home.

192
00:10:22,184 --> 00:10:26,084
But I'm helping out here.

193
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:29,114
You can't even play the organ.

194
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:33,164
You're of no use here.

195
00:10:35,494 --> 00:10:39,024
Oh? Are you two friends?

196
00:10:39,364 --> 00:10:40,834
No, we are not!

197
00:10:41,374 --> 00:10:46,674
Oh. Well in that case, this is Kiyokazu Fujimoto
who has been working here with me.

198
00:10:46,674 --> 00:10:48,814
And this is Kobato.

199
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:50,174
I'm counting on your help today.

200
00:10:50,444 --> 00:10:51,414
Yes ma'am!

201
00:10:53,914 --> 00:10:55,244
Don't get in my way.

202
00:10:58,224 --> 00:11:01,344
Mr. Kiyokazu, hurry up and play the organ!

203
00:11:01,924 --> 00:11:04,254
Hurry, teacher!

204
00:11:04,524 --> 00:11:06,584
You two keep them happy, all right?

205
00:11:15,104 --> 00:11:16,594
Kobato, come on!

206
00:11:16,704 --> 00:11:18,104
Let's dance!

207
00:11:24,284 --> 00:11:25,544
What in the world is that?

208
00:11:27,414 --> 00:11:30,444
This person is mean!

209
00:11:30,884 --> 00:11:32,644
But I'm not going to let that get to me!

210
00:11:35,294 --> 00:11:36,344
Wow!

211
00:11:36,494 --> 00:11:39,054
Kobato, you're funny!

212
00:12:15,564 --> 00:12:18,824
Is this a place where children live?

213
00:12:19,334 --> 00:12:21,234
They don't actually live here.

214
00:12:21,234 --> 00:12:23,504
We look after them during the day.

215
00:12:23,904 --> 00:12:25,204
I see.

216
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:29,144
But you know, this place is pretty old.

217
00:12:30,014 --> 00:12:35,954
With new kindergartens opening up nearby,
we're seeing fewer and fewer students.

218
00:12:39,784 --> 00:12:40,914
However!

219
00:12:41,994 --> 00:12:43,254
We'll just have to hang in there!

220
00:12:43,424 --> 00:12:46,984
Yep. Not worth worrying about.

221
00:12:47,264 --> 00:12:50,394
You're right. It's exactly as you say, Fujimoto.

222
00:12:51,504 --> 00:12:52,484
And thank you, Kobato.

223
00:12:52,704 --> 00:12:56,364
You were a great help today.
The children had a good time.

224
00:12:56,834 --> 00:12:58,244
Oh, no, I uh.

225
00:12:58,244 --> 00:13:00,714
I was just playing with them.

226
00:13:00,714 --> 00:13:03,504
I mean, Ioryogi-san always
gets angry with me and...

227
00:13:05,984 --> 00:13:08,644
Oh no! Ioryogi-san is gone!

228
00:13:09,154 --> 00:13:11,484
Oh, I didn't know you had someone with you.

229
00:13:11,484 --> 00:13:16,584
Yes! Uh, well I guess you wouldn't say
"someone," he's a stuffed animal person!

230
00:13:17,224 --> 00:13:21,284
Well he can't talk, so if I don't go
and get him, he'll scold me!

231
00:13:23,164 --> 00:13:24,534
Goodbye!

232
00:13:26,764 --> 00:13:29,294
Um... can I come again tomorrow?

233
00:13:29,774 --> 00:13:31,104
If it's alright with you...

234
00:13:31,104 --> 00:13:32,334
Ms. Sayaka.

235
00:13:32,774 --> 00:13:36,604
We have no idea where she's
from or what she does.

236
00:13:36,714 --> 00:13:38,704
Are you sure it's safe to let her in
and out of the kindergarten?

237
00:13:39,414 --> 00:13:40,914
You do know about me!

238
00:13:40,914 --> 00:13:42,574
My name is Kobato Hanato!

239
00:13:42,984 --> 00:13:46,014
You think your name says everything about you?

240
00:13:46,124 --> 00:13:47,244
I am...

241
00:13:47,424 --> 00:13:48,684
You're what?

242
00:13:53,124 --> 00:13:56,324
I'm in the middle of my search.

243
00:13:57,764 --> 00:13:58,854
Oh, my.

244
00:14:00,364 --> 00:14:03,334
Well then Kobato, if it's not inconvenient for
you, we'd be happy to have you here.

245
00:14:03,934 --> 00:14:07,344
We can't pay you very much, though.

246
00:14:07,974 --> 00:14:12,644
Oh no! If you would let me help,
that's plenty for me!

247
00:14:13,184 --> 00:14:14,844
Why thank you.

248
00:14:21,054 --> 00:14:22,084
Hey...

249
00:14:22,254 --> 00:14:23,624
Yes?

250
00:14:24,464 --> 00:14:26,054
Just one thing...

251
00:14:28,494 --> 00:14:30,734
If you're here out of sympathy or curiosity,
we don't need you.

252
00:14:30,734 --> 00:14:31,754
Huh?

253
00:14:32,904 --> 00:14:37,394
We're sick and tired of people feeling
sorry for us. It's uncalled-for.

254
00:14:37,604 --> 00:14:39,364
Well that's not how I feel!

255
00:14:47,984 --> 00:14:49,174
Um...

256
00:14:58,624 --> 00:14:59,954
Uncalled-for...

257
00:15:02,234 --> 00:15:04,424
You want to know what's uncalled-for?

258
00:15:05,934 --> 00:15:10,064
Suddenly leaving me alone in the
middle of town is uncalled-for!

259
00:15:11,144 --> 00:15:13,774
It's a good thing I found you, Ioryogi-san.

260
00:15:13,774 --> 00:15:15,034
No it isn't!

261
00:15:15,174 --> 00:15:17,914
Do you have any idea how hard it is to
move about a little bit at a time,

262
00:15:17,914 --> 00:15:19,114
trying not to be noticed?!

263
00:15:19,114 --> 00:15:20,634
I'm sorry!

264
00:15:20,914 --> 00:15:26,884
I told you didn't I? Here, I am a stuffed toy and
stuffed toys do not walk around on their own!

265
00:15:26,884 --> 00:15:28,514
I'm sorry!

266
00:15:29,394 --> 00:15:33,054
Never mind the bottle, you even
forgot to take me with you!

267
00:15:34,764 --> 00:15:35,924
The bottle!

268
00:15:39,104 --> 00:15:40,594
Just as I thought.

269
00:15:41,004 --> 00:15:42,704
What do you mean, just as you thought?

270
00:15:42,704 --> 00:15:45,004
Did you think there'd be something in there?

271
00:15:46,274 --> 00:15:52,074
I guess what I'm doing isn't
helping to heal anyone at all.

272
00:15:53,184 --> 00:15:54,244
In fact...

273
00:15:55,484 --> 00:15:57,004
I wonder if it's uncalled-for.

274
00:16:00,424 --> 00:16:03,824
Mr. Fujimoto looked hurt.

275
00:16:05,394 --> 00:16:09,494
But he said I was uncalled-for.

276
00:16:10,464 --> 00:16:13,494
Well. I guess it depends on the person.

277
00:16:14,734 --> 00:16:21,664
If there are people in the world who are hurt
and those who are not, of those who are,

278
00:16:22,414 --> 00:16:28,044
I hadn't realized that there are people who
want to be healed and those who don't.

279
00:16:29,514 --> 00:16:30,714
So?

280
00:16:31,424 --> 00:16:32,714
Yes?

281
00:16:32,924 --> 00:16:35,114
What do you want to do about it?

282
00:16:39,564 --> 00:16:41,224
I...

283
00:16:41,694 --> 00:16:45,694
You want to heal, don't you? Then go and heal!

284
00:16:46,634 --> 00:16:47,974
Would it be okay?

285
00:16:47,974 --> 00:16:51,804
Think about whether it was okay or
not after you've actually healed.

286
00:16:54,844 --> 00:16:56,174
Yes sir!

287
00:17:14,834 --> 00:17:16,294
Why that's...

288
00:17:19,164 --> 00:17:20,434
Toshihiko?

289
00:17:22,434 --> 00:17:23,904
Kobato!

290
00:17:24,074 --> 00:17:27,804
What about nursery school?
Are you on your way home?

291
00:17:30,074 --> 00:17:31,974
Mhm. But not yet.

292
00:17:36,214 --> 00:17:38,584
You like the swing?

293
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:46,894
No. It's not my favorite. But I've got to stay
here awhile longer until my mom gets back.

294
00:17:50,664 --> 00:17:52,294
She's working.

295
00:17:52,734 --> 00:17:54,394
She works, does she?

296
00:17:54,704 --> 00:17:55,864
But...

297
00:17:56,874 --> 00:17:59,374
My mom really works hard!

298
00:17:59,374 --> 00:18:03,974
It's hard because she got divorced,
but she still makes breakfast for me!

299
00:18:04,384 --> 00:18:06,844
And she's really kind! Really!

300
00:18:07,314 --> 00:18:09,044
That's great!

301
00:18:11,724 --> 00:18:14,344
Aren't you going to tell me how bad she is?

302
00:18:14,954 --> 00:18:16,394
Why is she bad?

303
00:18:27,264 --> 00:18:31,334
Toshihiko, is your mother late
coming to get you again?

304
00:18:31,904 --> 00:18:33,104
Uh-huh

305
00:18:33,104 --> 00:18:38,374
Oh... You're such a good boy,
Toshihiko, without even complaining.

306
00:18:40,414 --> 00:18:45,974
She's late again today too? You're such a
good child, Toshihiko. Patiently waiting.

307
00:18:48,254 --> 00:18:52,694
If only she would be more considerate
and put herself in Toshihiko's position.

308
00:18:52,764 --> 00:18:54,094
Really.

309
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:58,164
I mean I realize she's busy, but you know...

310
00:18:58,164 --> 00:19:00,934
It certainly is a problem.

311
00:19:02,804 --> 00:19:05,334
They all talk about what a bad mother she is.

312
00:19:05,804 --> 00:19:07,904
That she should do better.

313
00:19:08,874 --> 00:19:11,544
Is she a bad mother?

314
00:19:11,544 --> 00:19:15,034
No way! She's doing everything she can!

315
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:18,644
Really! She's awesome! She's the best!

316
00:19:24,294 --> 00:19:25,594
That's wonderful!

317
00:19:30,594 --> 00:19:33,154
Your awesome mom who works hard...

318
00:19:33,734 --> 00:19:34,994
I think she's super!

319
00:19:36,674 --> 00:19:38,034
Really?

320
00:19:38,444 --> 00:19:40,904
Yes. She's a wonderful mother.

321
00:19:54,254 --> 00:19:56,084
Wh-What's the matter?!

322
00:19:59,464 --> 00:20:01,554
Does it hurt somewhere?

323
00:20:02,464 --> 00:20:03,794
No!

324
00:20:05,004 --> 00:20:06,194
Really?

325
00:20:08,774 --> 00:20:09,734
Yes...

326
00:20:35,394 --> 00:20:37,224
What?!

327
00:20:39,904 --> 00:20:44,274
Th-There's something in here! But, but... why?!

328
00:20:44,674 --> 00:20:47,034
That must have belonged to Toshihiko.

329
00:20:48,174 --> 00:20:49,644
Toshihiko?

330
00:20:57,254 --> 00:20:59,374
You can do it, Kobato!

331
00:21:12,864 --> 00:21:17,704
I think you made him happy, saying nice things
about his mother and being nice to him yourself.

332
00:21:21,714 --> 00:21:25,644
Huh? Do you think I was kind to him?

333
00:21:26,814 --> 00:21:28,884
No matter how kindly you treat someone,

334
00:21:28,884 --> 00:21:31,074
if you're looking for something in
return, you'll never be healing.

335
00:21:31,854 --> 00:21:34,654
Just do what you want to do
and I think you'll be all right.

336
00:21:38,364 --> 00:21:39,584
Yes.

337
00:21:40,794 --> 00:21:43,994
I am going to work hard at collecting
people's broken hearts!

338
00:21:44,964 --> 00:21:46,134
Wait a minute!

339
00:21:46,134 --> 00:21:48,534
You're sounding like you're going to go
around breaking people's hearts

340
00:21:48,534 --> 00:21:50,264
so you can collect them.

341
00:21:50,534 --> 00:21:52,974
Should I say I'm going to collect healed hearts?

342
00:21:53,574 --> 00:21:57,704
That sounds like you're going to heal
the heart and then take it away.

343
00:21:57,814 --> 00:22:01,644
Then what should I call this thing I just received?

344
00:22:02,254 --> 00:22:04,624
Oh what a nuisance!

345
00:22:04,624 --> 00:22:08,054
That looks like a kompeito candy
so just call it kompeito!

346
00:22:09,794 --> 00:22:17,024
Kompeito... okay. I'm going
to call these kompeito.

347
00:22:18,264 --> 00:22:19,494
Hey Kobato!

348
00:22:19,664 --> 00:22:20,864
Yes?

349
00:22:28,414 --> 00:22:33,674
Leaving me behind was out of the question, but
for being your first time, you did very well.

350
00:22:33,784 --> 00:22:36,474
So I'm going to give you a bonus. You get a
score of one hundred points today!

351
00:22:38,654 --> 00:22:41,084
And we're going to keep it up,
aren't we, Kobato?

352
00:22:41,594 --> 00:22:44,684
Yes sir! Kobato is ready!

353
00:22:45,794 --> 00:22:48,784
Oh but, you're not going to let the hundred
points get to your head, now are you?

354
00:22:48,934 --> 00:22:51,364
Huh? But you're always
telling me to use my head.

355
00:22:51,364 --> 00:22:53,104
That's not what I meant!

356
00:22:53,104 --> 00:22:55,534
Well then what did you mean?

357
00:22:55,534 --> 00:22:58,244
Never mind. I'm taking the hundred points back!

358
00:22:58,244 --> 00:23:00,364
What?! No way!

359
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

360
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

361
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

362
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

363
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Jibun no kage wo

364
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

365
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
Sore nara

366
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

367
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

368
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

369
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

370
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
Shinpai nante iranai yo

371
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Issho ni iru kara

372
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

373
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:25,964
Fushigi da

374
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...A Gift from the Rain.
Fushigi da

375
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,754
Next episode
...A Gift from the Rain.

